/-!
# Local complete intersection rings

A Noetherian local ring `A` is a *complete intersection* when its completion `A^` at the maximal
ideal is a quotient of a regular local ring by an ideal generated by a regular sequence, and a
Noetherian ring is a *local complete intersection* when all of its local rings are complete
intersections. These are intrinsic notions: no base ring is involved, in contrast with the
relative notions `IsCompleteIntersection k A` and `IsLocalCompleteIntersection k S` of an algebra
over a field. This file sets up the intrinsic notions and relates them to the relative ones.

The condition is well posed because it does not depend on the presentation: for a Noetherian
complete local ring `A`, if the kernel of *one* surjection onto `A` from a regular local ring is
generated by a regular sequence, then the kernel of *every* such surjection is. Two presentations
`R ↠ A` and `S ↠ A` of a complete local ring are dominated by a common presentation by a power
series ring, and the regular-sequence condition is detected by the numerical identity
`dim A + μ(ker f) = dim R`, which is insensitive to completing `R`.

The main computation is a characterization of quotients of a regular ring. Let `R` be regular, let
`p` be a prime of `R`, let `I ⊆ p` be an ideal and let `A = R_p/I R_p`. Then `A^` is a complete
intersection if and only if `I R_p` is generated by a regular sequence, if and only if the
conormal module of `I R_p` is generated by `dim R_p - dim A` elements. Combined with the
comparison of a finite type algebra over a field with its presentations, this shows that for such
an algebra the relative and intrinsic notions agree.

All declarations below are in the namespace `LocalCompleteIntersection`.

## Main definitions

* `IsCompleteIntersectionRing` — a Noetherian local ring whose completion at the maximal ideal is
  a regular local ring modulo a regular sequence.
* `IsLocalCompleteIntersectionRing` — a Noetherian ring all of whose localizations at primes are
  complete intersection local rings.
* `IsCompleteIntersectionCompleteLocalRing` — the presentation-free condition on a Noetherian
  complete local ring of being a regular local ring modulo a regular sequence.

## Main results

* `isCompleteIntersectionCompleteLocalRing_adicCompletion_quotientAtPrime` — the completion of
  `R_p/(rs)R_p` is a complete intersection, for `R` regular and `rs` a regular sequence inside `p`.
* `forall_regularPresentation_iff_exists` — the regular-sequence condition on the kernel holds for
  every presentation of a Noetherian complete local ring by a regular local ring as soon as it
  holds for one.
* `quotient_regular_ring_tfae` — the three characterizations of a quotient of a regular ring whose
  completed localization is a complete intersection.
* `isCompleteIntersectionRing_of_ringEquiv` — the complete intersection condition on a Noetherian
  local ring transports along a ring isomorphism.
* `isCompleteIntersection_atPrime_iff_isCompleteIntersectionRing` and
  `isLocalCompleteIntersection_iff_isLocalCompleteIntersectionRing` — for a finite type algebra
  over a field, the relative notions over the field agree with the intrinsic ones.

## Implementation notes

A presentation is a surjective ring homomorphism; onto a nonzero local ring it is automatically
local, so no separate hypothesis is needed. Generation of an ideal by a regular sequence is
expressed by a list `rs` with `RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular R rs` and
`Ideal.ofList rs = RingHom.ker f`. In `IsCompleteIntersectionRing` the presenting regular local
ring is required to live in the same universe as the ring being presented, and local rings of a
general ring are the canonical localizations `Localization.AtPrime p`. Codimensions are written
without truncated subtraction, as the existence of `c : ℕ` with `dim A + c = dim R`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09PZ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09PZ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09Q0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09Q0)
